# There is nothing here to configure.
#
# The DHUN web app builds and runs with **no environment variable at all**: no
# API key, no token, no account, no endpoint baked into a build, no analytics
# id. That is a design constraint, not an oversight — the project operates no
# backend, and a build that needed a secret could not be published from a static
# host for free.
#
# `.env` files are not read by any tool in this repository. This file exists so
# that a contributor looking for one finds the answer instead of a blank space,
# and so that `.gitignore`'s allowance for a sanitized example file is used
# rather than left as a mystery.
#
# The one environment variable anywhere in the web workstream is the development
# server's optional port, and it is read as a plain shell variable — there is no
# loader involved:
#
#     PORT=4173 npm run dev          # from the repository root
#     PORT=8080 npm --prefix app-web run dev
#
# It defaults to 4173 when unset, and it has no effect on the built app: the
# published files are static and carry no configuration.
